      <div class="choice-detail">We read the course expectations together and you ask anything you want about how the year works. Bring up the parts that seem unfair or unclear now rather than in November.</div>
    </div>
    <div class="choice">
      <div class="choice-letter">3</div>
      <div class="choice-title">Practical set-up</div>
      <div class="choice-detail">Join Google Classroom, find your class Drive folder, and sign in to the class AI platform. <strong>The Classroom join code is on the board, not on this page.</strong> This site is public, so anything that is only for our class stays in the room. If you are absent today, ask for the code next class.</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="callout activity">
    <div class="callout-title">Where we live, and what we owe it</div>
    <p>Back to the video. Four questions, as a whole class, in this order:</p>
    <ol>
      <li>How do you feel after watching that?</li>
      <li>What does it imply for us, as humans on Earth?</li>
      <li>What role do we have in looking after the environment, and what responsibility comes with it?</li>
      <li>What commitment do we want to hold, as a class, for our home?</li>
    </ol>
    <p>The first question has no wrong answer and every answer gets heard. The last one we write down together, in our own words. That becomes the commitment this class holds for the year, and we come back to it: at the end of Unit 4 when you have the climate science, and again in Unit 6 when you redesign a piece of Chennai.</p>
  </div>
